  "retainedCorrections": [
    "The first differential grouped shared callback source locations as test-file identities. Named scenario suites now identify reference results; original failed comparison retained.",
    "The first maximum-duration test also overflowed the pinned reference timer. The final boundary remains large enough to overflow an unchunked parent guard while staying below the reference limit; the original reference failure remains retained.",
    "Review found immediate shortened deadlines, beforeAll slow annotations and large parent timers needed corrections.",
    "Review found late fixture use could reopen during cleanup and known fixture errors could disappear after cleanup expiration. Dedicated controls now cover both fixes.",
    "The first native reference control passed lifecycle assertions but failed server shutdown because Bun closeAllConnections had already stopped the server. The final owner awaits ordinary server.close.",
    "The second native reference retry exceeded its deliberately short 500ms timeout during click. The final shared test extends only the retry budget to 10 seconds; the initial attempt still times out at 500ms."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Independent runner remains internal. Public CLI/configuration, serial retries, reporters and artifact integration remain open.",
    "Native controls cover a pending evaluation and normal context/browser closure, not every blocked renderer/driver or artifact cancellation path.",
    "Parent phase recovery of a blocked event loop and existing process-group escalation pass host controls; this does not establish exhaustive descendant custody.",
    "Application admission uses the private adapter and its existing matcher/step bridge. Only TodoMVC and SVGOMG, Bun, one/four workers, stock and private accelerated Chromium are covered here.",
    "The raw application selected-input receipts bind runner source/build and adapter files; they are not complete release or final performance manifests.",
    "Native fixture source and executable hashes are retained; no complete platform or browser distribution refresh.",
    "No new performance claim or final majority-scenario 2x acceptance."
  ],
